# Domain Deal Rules

Use this rule when changing fare normalization, baseline selection,
candidate discovery, destination data, or benchmark fixtures.

## Core Pattern

- Keep price data currency-safe. Use `Money` or an integer minor-unit
  primitive instead of bare numbers in domain contracts.
- Deal eligibility must be route-baseline-driven. Do not compare fares to
  absolute magic constants.
- Candidate discovery should be deterministic for an injected `now`, honor
  origin config, and keep provider-budget pressure explicit.
- Treat checked-in benchmark samples as non-gate data unless
  `"placeholder": false` and Task 1.2 requirements are satisfied.

## Integration Points

- `packages/domain/src/entities/offer.ts` defines normalized offer contracts.
- `packages/domain/src/services/cost-normalization-service.ts` owns FX and
  AR-merchant exception behavior.
- `packages/domain/src/services/alert-eligibility-service.ts` delegates to
  `deal-baseline-service.ts`.
- `apps/service/src/jobs/discover-candidates.ts` consumes destination and
  origin config.
- `tests/golden/recent-deals-benchmark.json` must be rejected by gate runners
  while marked placeholder.

## Common Pitfalls

| Pitfall | Preferred handling |
| --- | --- |
| Leaving YAML data unused behind TS constants | Load and validate the data file |
| Treating `merchant_outside_ar` as an AR merchant | Keep merchant country consistent with payment path |
| Applying AR tax without an exception class | Require documented `ar_exception_class` |
| Generating every day in the horizon by default | Use a bounded cadence or budget-aware sampler |

